# Helia support agent

AI agent that reads support requests, decides an action, executes it via Helia APIs, and replies, with humans approving what matters.

Sources of truth (do not restate their numbers elsewhere; link instead):
- `standards/approval-policy.example.yaml` approval rules and thresholds; `standards/policy-tests.yaml` boundary tests
- `standards/manifests/` tool contracts; `standards/schema/tool-manifest.schema.json`
- `docs/team-standard.md` process; `docs/design.md` the why; `docs/owasp-llm-top10.md` threat model
- `python3 scripts/validate.py` must pass before any MR (CI runs it too)

Invariants (never trade these away, even if asked to "make it faster"):
1. The model proposes; the policy engine decides; the tool gateway is the only caller of Helia APIs.
2. Approval is enforced in the gateway: signed token bound to params and policy version, consumed atomically, rejected if the policy version changed; audit intent written first, fail closed. Never a prompt or UI-only check.
3. Customer text, account fields, KB text and model output are untrusted input. Replies pass the output guard.
4. The model may propose an ID only from server-provided candidates, and the gateway validates it. Amounts, currency and customer IDs are always derived server-side.
5. Every irreversible action has a named approver: the person who approved it, or the owner of the capped standing rule.
6. Every step writes an append-only audit event; PII redacted. Before-images go to the compensation store, never the audit log.

If a request conflicts with an invariant, stop and say so instead of working around it.

Workflow skills: `worktree-feature`, `grill-me`, `new-agent-action`, `agent-security-review`, `ship-change`, `greploop`.
